    "Sanhedrin 52b_3-3": {
      "index": 43,
      "page_ref": "Sanhedrin 52b",
      "start_segment": 3,
      "end_segment": 3,
      "classification_shown": "YES",
      "mishnah_withheld": false,
      "detector_version": "v14",
      "applies_to": "base",
      "is_story": "yes",
      "extent": null,
      "confidence": null,
      "grouping": null,
      "display_problem": false,
      "quote": "",
      "quote_polarity": null,
      "quote_start": "",
      "quote_end": "",
      "notes": "continues: The Gemara asks: Did Rabbi Elazar ben Tzadok say that to the Sages, and did the Sages answer him in that manner? But isn’t a different version of the exchange taught in a baraita: Rabbi Elazar, son of Rabbi Tzadok, says: I remember when I was a child, and was riding on my father’s shoulders. And they brought a priest’s daughter who had committed adultery, and surrounded her with bundles of branches and burned her. The Sages said to him: You were a minor at that time and one cannot bring proof from the testimony of a minor, as perhaps you did not understand the proceedings properly. The two versions of this exchange do not accord with each other. The Gemara answers: There were two separate incidents, and Rabbi Elazar ben Tzadok testified with regard to both. | הָכִי אֲמַר לְהוּ, וְהָכִי אַהְדַּרוּ לֵיהּ? וְהָתַנְיָא, אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בְּרַבִּי צָדוֹק: זְכוּרַנִי כְּשֶׁהָיִיתִי תִּינוֹק וּמוּרְכָּב עַל כְּתֵיפוֹ שֶׁל אַבָּא, וְהֵבִיאוּ בַּת כֹּהֵן שֶׁזִּינְּתָה וְהִקִּיפוּהָ חֲבִילֵי זְמוֹרוֹת וּשְׂרָפוּהָ. אָמְרוּ לוֹ: קָטָן הָיִיתָ, וְאֵין מְבִיאִין רְאָיָה מִן הַקָּטָן. שְׁנֵי מַעֲשִׂים הֲווֹ.\n\n",
      "schema_version": "axes-3",
      "answered_at": "2026-11-12T04:36:00.785Z",
      "stratum": "aggadic",
      "biblical": false
    },
